@node User Option Reference
@section User Option Reference
@cindex user options
@vindex user options

Every user option defined with @code{defcustom} under @file{lisp/},
in alphabetical order.  Set them with
@kbd{M-x customize-group @key{RET} beads} or by adding a
@code{setopt} call to your init file.

@defopt beads-actor
Actor name for audit trail.
If nil, uses the $USER environment variable.  This value is used
for tracking who performs actions in the issue tracker.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-agent-shell-config
Agent config to use for beads-agent sessions.
If nil, uses ‘agent-shell-preferred-agent-config’ if set,
otherwise prompts user to select from ‘agent-shell-agent-configs’.
See ‘agent-shell-make-agent-config’ for config format.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-claudemacs-tool
Which claudemacs tool to use for agent sessions.
Must be a symbol registered in ‘claudemacs-tool-registry’.
Common values are ‘claude’, ‘codex’, or ‘gemini’.
Default: @code{claude}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-curated-backends
Backends shown directly in the agent launch UI.
Backends not listed here stay registered and selectable, but the
launch menu places them behind an ‘... other’ overflow (the backend
list is curated, not truncated).  Names are matched against the
backend ‘name’ slot; a name that is not registered is ignored.

‘mock’ is a test-only backend and is never shown in the user menu.
Default: @code{("claude-code" "agent-shell" "terminal")}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-default-backend
Default backend to use for agent sessions.
If nil, prompt user to select from available backends.
If set to a backend name string, use that backend automatically.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-default-terminal
Default ‘beads-terminal’ subclass symbol for agent spawning.
Governs the agent terminal spawn path (the class-valued knob),
distinct from the symbol-valued ‘beads-terminal-backend’ which
governs one-shot ‘bd’ command execution.  Both coexist for one
release; see NEWS.
Default: @code{beads-terminal-auto}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-display-show-instance
When non-nil, append #N to icons in narrow display contexts.

By default the instance number is shown only in mode-line, the
agent list buffer, and help-echo tooltips, freeing space in the
issue list column and dashboard badges.  Set this to t to also
show #N in those tight surfaces.

Note: the agent list buffer (‘*beads-agents*’) always shows
instance numbers regardless of this setting — that buffer is the
canonical place to disambiguate parallel sessions and dedicates
column width specifically to the ‘#N’ suffix.  See
‘beads-agent-list--format-type’.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-display-type-icons
Per-type icon overrides for agent display.

Alist mapping lowercase type names to display strings.  Each entry
takes precedence over the ‘icon’ slot of the corresponding
‘beads-agent-type’.  When an entry is present with a nil value the
type’s icon resolves to nil (and renderers fall back to the letter)
without consulting the slot.  Set the whole variable to nil to
disable all overrides and use only class slots.

Example:
  (("task" . "🛠") ("review" . "🔍"))
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-display-use-icons
Whether to use emoji icons for agent type indicators.

Controls what ‘beads-agent-type-icon-or-letter’ returns: an emoji
icon (from the ‘icon’ slot or a ‘beads-agent-display-type-icons’ override)
or the single-letter abbreviation from the ‘letter’ slot.

Possible values:
- ‘auto’ (default): icons under GUI Emacs, letters in TTY frames
- t: always use icons regardless of frame type
- nil: always use single letters (T/R/P/Q/C)

Set this to nil when icons render as tofu (missing-glyph) on your
system, or override icons per-type via ‘beads-agent-display-type-icons’.
Default: @code{auto}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-eca-buffer-pattern
Pattern to match ECA chat buffer names.
ECA chat buffers typically use angle brackets with session info:
  <eca-chat:N:M> where N is session ID and M is buffer number.
Default: @code{"<eca-chat"}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-list-backend-width
Width of Backend column in agent list.
Default: @code{15}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-list-directory-width
Width of Directory column in agent list.
Default: @code{30}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-list-duration-width
Width of Duration column in agent list.
Default: @code{10}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-list-issue-width
Width of Issue ID column in agent list.
Default: @code{16}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-list-status-width
Width of Status column in agent list.
Default: @code{10}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-list-title-width
Width of Title column in agent list.
Default: @code{30}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-list-type-width
Width of Type column in agent list.
Holds the agent role icon (or single-letter fallback) plus the
‘#N’ instance suffix (e.g. "🦅#1" or "T#1").  The default of 8
leaves headroom for multi-digit instance numbers like ‘#10’ under
GUI Emacs where the emoji occupies two display columns.
Default: @code{8}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-mode-line-faces
When non-nil, use faces for mode-line indicator.
When nil, use plain text without face properties.
Default: @code{t}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-mode-line-format
Format for the mode-line indicator.
The value can be one of:
  - ‘default’: Show [project:agent@@context] format
  - ‘compact’: Show just [P:T#1] minimal format
  - ‘full’: Show full project path and agent details
  - A function: Called with no arguments, returns a string or nil
Default: @code{default}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-mode-line-mode
Non-nil if Beads-Agent-Mode-Line mode is enabled.
See the ‘beads-agent-mode-line-mode’ command
for a description of this minor mode.
Setting this variable directly does not take effect;
either customize it (see the info node ‘Easy Customization’)
or call the function ‘beads-agent-mode-line-mode’.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-mode-line-mode-hook
Hook run after entering or leaving ‘beads-agent-mode-line-mode’.
No problems result if this variable is not bound.
‘add-hook’ automatically binds it.  (This is true for all hook variables.)
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-plan-backend
Preferred backend for Plan agents.
If nil, uses ‘beads-agent-default-backend’ or first available.
Set to a backend name string to prefer a specific backend for Plan agents.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-plan-prompt
System (role) prompt for the Plan agent.
Role-only as of the Phase 1a-ii split; the issue envelope and the
‘bd update’ output block live in ‘beads-agent-type-plan--user-prompt’.
A user-customised value is delivered via the backend’s
system-prompt channel with placeholders still substituted (see NEWS
for the old default verbatim).
Default: @code{"You are a planning agent. Create a detailed implementation plan WITH...}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-review-backend
Preferred backend for Review agents.
If nil, uses ‘beads-agent-default-backend’ or first available.
Set to a backend name string to prefer a specific backend for Review agents.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-review-prompt
System (role) prompt for the Review agent.
Role-only as of the Phase 1a-ii split: the issue envelope and the
‘bd update’ output block now live in the Review *user* prompt
(‘beads-agent-type-review--user-prompt’).  A user-customised value
is delivered via the backend’s system-prompt channel; any embedded
<ISSUE-ID>/<ISSUE-TITLE>/<ISSUE-DESCRIPTION> placeholders are still
substituted (see NEWS for the old default verbatim).
Default: @code{"You are a code review agent. # Constraints - Read-only: DO NOT modif...}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-review-qa-prompt
System (role) prompt for the Review agent in QA mode.
This is the former ‘beads-agent-qa-prompt’, relocated onto the
Review QA path when the standalone QA class was removed (F3).
Role-only: the issue envelope and the ‘bd update’ output block live
in ‘beads-agent-type-review--qa-user-prompt’.  A user-customised
value is delivered via the backend’s system-prompt channel with
placeholders still substituted.
Default: @code{"You are a QA agent. # Constraints - Testing focus: Run tests, verify...}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-session-restart-delay
Delay in seconds before restarting a session.
This allows cleanup to complete before starting a new agent.
Default: @code{0.5}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-task-backend
Preferred backend for Task agents.
If nil, uses ‘beads-agent-default-backend’ or first available.
Set to a backend name string to prefer a specific backend for Task agents.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-use-worktrees
Whether agent sessions use git worktrees for isolation.
Each issue gets its own worktree, named after the issue ID.
Worktrees are created in a sibling directory to the main repo.

Possible values:
- t: Always use worktrees for agent sessions (default)
- nil: Never use worktrees, agents work in the main repo
- 'ask: Prompt the user each time whether to use a worktree
Default: @code{t}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-agent-worktree-parent
Parent directory for agent worktrees.
If nil, worktrees are created as siblings to the main repository.
For example, if the repo is at ~/projects/myrepo, worktrees are
created at ~/projects/issue-id/.

If set to a path, worktrees are created under that directory.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-auto-refresh
Automatically refresh buffers after mutations.
When enabled, beads list and show buffers will automatically
refresh after operations like create, update, or close.
Default: @code{t}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-command-async-max-concurrent
Concurrency limit for ‘beads-command-execute-async’ when ‘:queue’ is honoured.

Values:
  ‘auto’      — resolve from ‘beads-command--policy’ probe (the default).
  integer N   — at most N processes in flight at once (overrides probe).
  ‘unlimited’ — no cap (legacy / single-shot callers).

A user override to an integer trumps the probe — set this to 1 to
force serial execution even on ‘server-mode’ Dolt.
Default: @code{auto}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-command-async-timeout
Default timeout in seconds for ‘beads-command-execute-async’ callers.

When ‘:timeout’ is supplied to ‘beads-command-execute-async’ the
process is auto-killed and ‘on-error’ is invoked with a timeout
condition.  Callers that do not specify ‘:timeout’ opt out of timeout
handling entirely.  The dashboard always passes this default.
Default: @code{10}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-completion-mode
Non-nil if Beads-Completion mode is enabled.
See the ‘beads-completion-mode’ command
for a description of this minor mode.
Setting this variable directly does not take effect;
either customize it (see the info node ‘Easy Customization’)
or call the function ‘beads-completion-mode’.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-completion-mode-hook
Hook run after entering or leaving ‘beads-completion-mode’.
No problems result if this variable is not bound.
‘add-hook’ automatically binds it.  (This is true for all hook variables.)
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-completion-show-unavailable-backends
Whether to show unavailable backends in completion lists.
When non-nil, unavailable backends are shown but cannot be selected.
They appear grayed out and are grouped separately from available backends.
When nil, only available backends appear in the completion list.

This affects ‘beads-agent-start’ and related functions that prompt
for backend selection.
Default: @code{t}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-dashboard-auto-refresh-interval
Seconds of Emacs idle time between auto-refresh ticks.
Auto-refresh is OFF by default and toggled with ‘r’ in the dashboard.
Default: @code{30}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-dashboard-city
Name of the owning city to show in the dashboard header, or nil.
When nil, a dashboard opened for a Gas City store falls back to the
basename of the GC_CITY environment variable; otherwise the header
falls back to the resolved store path.  A caller can also scope a
board explicitly with the ‘:city’ keyword of ‘beads-dashboard’ (the
seam a city/rig integration uses to disambiguate two same-named rigs).
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-dashboard-default-collapsed
Alist mapping section keys to t when they should default-collapsed.
Sections collapsed by default do not fetch their data until expanded.
Defaults expand every actionable section so the project pulse is
visible at a glance; only Federation (server-mode only) starts
collapsed because most projects do not use it.
Default: @code{((federation . t))}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-dashboard-live-auto-attach
Whether opening a dashboard attaches to its store’s live journal.
When non-nil and ‘beads-live’ is available, a local dashboard attaches
on mount and detaches on kill so journal records update it in place.
Remote stores are never auto-attached here: the synchronous capability
probe would touch the host at mount time, which the remote render guard
forbids.  Bind to nil in batch/tests that must not start a stream.
Default: @code{t}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-dashboard-section-batch
Rows added to a section per ‘beads-dashboard-load-more’ invocation.
Also the step used by ‘beads-dashboard-load-less’.  Must be at least 1
— values of 0 or below make load-more a no-op and load-less immediately
floor every section.
Default: @code{10}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-dashboard-section-limit
Maximum number of issues rendered per dashboard section.

When a section has more issues than this limit, only the first N are
rendered and a ‘… and M more’ line is appended.  Set to nil to render
every issue (the section header always shows the full count).

Applies to: Stale, Orphans, In Flight, Ready, Blocked, Recently
Closed, and the Epic Progress list.
Default: @code{5}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-database-path
Path to the beads database.
If nil, bd will auto-discover the database by searching for a
.beads directory in the project hierarchy.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-debug-level
Debug logging level.
- ‘error’: Only log errors
- ‘info’: Log commands and important events (default)
- ‘verbose’: Log everything including command output
Default: @code{info}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-dolt-port
TCP port of the Dolt server for bd commands.
When set to an integer, beads.el injects BEADS_DOLT_PORT=<port>
into the process environment for every bd command.  This ensures
bd connects to the specified Dolt server instead of auto-starting
its own instance or relying on metadata.json in the .beads
directory.

Set this to the port of your shared Dolt server, e.g.:
  (setq beads-dolt-port 3307)

If nil, beads.el does not inject BEADS_DOLT_PORT, and bd uses its
normal discovery order: BEADS_DOLT_PORT env var, then metadata.json,
then auto-start.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-eldoc-cache-ttl
Seconds a fetched issue stays in the eldoc cache.
Default: @code{300}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-eldoc-directory
Store directory eldoc resolves ids in, or nil for ‘default-directory’.
Either a directory (a TRAMP name is fine; it is localized before
reaching ‘bd --directory’), or a function called with the issue id
that returns such a directory or nil.  Meant to be set buffer-locally
by callers that know which store owns an id -- gascity.el maps an id
prefix to its rig’s store -- so a terminal buffer sitting in one rig
still resolves another rig’s ids.  Also part of the cache scope.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-eldoc-issue-pattern
Regexp overriding ‘beads-issue-id-regexp’ for eldoc, or nil.
Group 1 must be the id.  Nil uses the shared regexp, which knows that
real ids are base-36 (bs-lc1lb, gce-hck), not hexadecimal.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-eldoc-issue-prefixes
Issue id prefixes to recognise in text, or nil for any.
A list of strings such as ("bde" "gce").  The base-36 id syntax
also matches ordinary hyphenated words ("post-command"), so a caller
that knows which stores are in play -- gascity.el knows every rig’s
prefix -- sets this buffer-locally and eldoc/reference detection then
ignores everything else.  Nil accepts any syntactically valid id.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-eldoc-mode
Non-nil if Beads-Eldoc mode is enabled.
See the ‘beads-eldoc-mode’ command
for a description of this minor mode.
Setting this variable directly does not take effect;
either customize it (see the info node ‘Easy Customization’)
or call the function ‘beads-eldoc-mode’.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-eldoc-mode-hook
Hook run after entering or leaving ‘beads-eldoc-mode’.
No problems result if this variable is not bound.
‘add-hook’ automatically binds it.  (This is true for all hook variables.)
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-eldoc-negative-cache-ttl
Seconds an unknown id stays cached as missing.
Terminal and log text is full of tokens that look like ids
("post-command", "gc-agent"), and each unknown one used to cost a
‘bd show’ per eldoc tick.  A miss is now remembered for this long, so
an unknown token spawns at most one lookup per interval and scope.
Default: @code{45}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-enable-debug
Enable debug logging to *beads-debug* buffer.
When enabled, all bd commands and their output will be logged
for troubleshooting purposes.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-event-fold-bucket
Seconds per churn bucket in ‘beads-event-fold’ (default 15 minutes).
Non-signal records with the same issue and op inside one bucket
coalesce into a single ‘×N’ row.
Default: @code{900}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-event-levels
Signal level of a journal op: (REGEXP . LEVEL), first match wins.
LEVEL is ‘attention’ or ‘watch’; an op no entry matches is a plain
event, and a plain ‘update’ whose diff is all bookkeeping drops back
to plain (‘beads-event-noise-fields’).  A signal event is never folded
into a churn row (‘beads-event-fold’).
Default: @code{(("\\`close\\'" . attention) ("\\`delete\\'" . attention) ("\\`dep_ad...}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-event-noise-fields
