@defopt beads-swarm-window-step
Rows added by ‘]’ when widening a clipped status-board group.
Default: @code{25}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-terminal-backend
Backend to use for interactive one-shot ‘bd’ command execution.

Deprecated (Phase 3): this symbol-valued knob is superseded by the
unified ‘beads-terminal’ spawn vocabulary.  It is still honoured for
back-compat — ‘beads-command--run-in-terminal’ resolves it through
‘beads-terminal--symbol->class’ and delegates to
‘beads-terminal-spawn’ — but new configuration should prefer the
class-valued terminal selection (‘beads-agent-default-terminal’ for
agents).  Expect this symbol-valued option to be removed in a future
release.

This knob governs ‘beads-command--run-in-terminal’ ONLY (running a
single ‘bd’ command in a terminal).  The agent spawn path is
governed by the class-valued ‘beads-agent-default-terminal’.

When nil (auto-detect), tries backends in order: vterm, eat, term.
The first available backend is used.

Available backends:
- nil: Auto-detect best available backend (vterm > eat > term).
- ‘vterm’: Use vterm (libvterm-based terminal).
- ‘eat’: Use Eat (Emulate A Terminal).
- ‘term’: Use built-in ‘term-mode’ terminal emulator.
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-terminal-tmux-backend
Terminal backend for attaching to a tmux session.
The actual spawn is delegated to beads.el’s terminal module
(‘beads-terminal-spawn’); this choice selects which backend class it
uses.  When nil, auto-detect the best available backend: ghostel when
it is installed (attempted/loaded, not merely already ‘featurep’ — see
‘beads-terminal-tmux--ghostel-available-p’), otherwise vterm > eat > term.

- nil:   auto-detect (ghostel when installed, then vterm, eat, term).
- vterm: requires the ‘vterm’ package.
- eat:   requires the ‘eat’ package.
- term:  the built-in ‘term-mode’ (always available).
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-terminal-tmux-ensure-mouse
When non-nil, ensure tmux mouse scrolling for attached sessions.
The attach pre-step turns the session’s tmux ‘mouse’ option on
(session-scoped) and installs a copy-mode ‘WheelDownPane’ binding that
leaves copy mode when it is already at the bottom.  Killing the
terminal buffer restores both.  Set to nil to leave tmux’s mouse
configuration untouched.
Default: @code{t}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-terminal-tmux-mode-line-status
When non-nil, mirror a tmux session’s status bar in the mode line.
On attaching, the session’s own tmux status bar is turned off (scoped
to the session) and the same information — the friendly session name
from ‘status-left’ and the window list — is rendered as a buffer-local
mode-line segment.  The change is reverted when the terminal buffer is
killed.  Set to nil to leave tmux’s status bar untouched.
Default: @code{t}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-terminal-tmux-preload-idle
Seconds of idle before the terminal backend preload, or nil to disable.
The preload loads the backend library ahead of the first attach, on
genuine idle time, so the one-off cost is not paid while typing.
Default: @code{10}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-terminal-tmux-remote-term
Fallback TERM for the remote side of a tmux attach, or nil for none.
A remote attach runs ‘ssh -t HOST … tmux attach …’, and ssh forwards
the TERM the local terminal backend advertises (e.g. ghostel’s
"xterm-ghostty").  A host with no terminfo entry for that name makes
the remote tmux client exit instantly; when the host appears to lack
the entry (a best-effort probe, ‘beads-remote-terminfo-p’), this TERM
is forced onto the remote command line instead.  Purely local attaches
never touch TERM — the terminal backend owns it.
Default: @code{"xterm-256color"}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-terminal-tmux-scroll-mode-hook
Hook run after entering or leaving ‘beads-terminal-tmux-scroll-mode’.
No problems result if this variable is not bound.
‘add-hook’ automatically binds it.  (This is true for all hook variables.)
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-terminal-tmux-status-interval
Seconds between refreshes of the tmux status mode-line segment.
Only consulted when ‘beads-terminal-tmux-mode-line-status’ is non-nil;
values at or below zero fall back to 5.
Default: @code{5}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-terminal-tmux-unshadow-minor-modes
Global minor modes whose keymaps are neutralised in terminal buffers.
Each named mode is given an empty keymap in the terminal buffer’s
‘minor-mode-overriding-map-alist’, so its bindings are suppressed in
that buffer only and the backend’s own key forwarding wins.  Set to nil
to touch no keymaps at all.
Default: @code{(pixel-scroll-precision-mode)}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-terminal-tmux-wheel-mode-hook
Hook run after entering or leaving ‘beads-terminal-tmux-wheel-mode’.
No problems result if this variable is not bound.
‘add-hook’ automatically binds it.  (This is true for all hook variables.)
Default: @code{nil}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-wisp-age-width
Width of the Age column in the wisp list.
Default: @code{12}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-wisp-id-width
Width of the Id column in the wisp list.
Default: @code{20}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-wisp-old-seconds
Age in seconds after which a wisp is considered old.
Old wisps have not been updated in this many seconds (24 hours by
default) and are candidates for ‘bd mol wisp gc’.  See
‘beads-wisp-kind’.
Default: @code{86400}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-wisp-phase-width
Width of the Phase column in the wisp list.
Default: @code{12}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-wisp-started-width
Width of the Started column in the wisp list.
Default: @code{9}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-wisp-status-width
Width of the Status column in the wisp list.
Default: @code{12}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-wisp-type-width
Width of the Type column in the wisp list.
Default: @code{10}.
@end defopt

@defopt beads-wisp-updated-width
Width of the Updated column in the wisp list.
Default: @code{9}.
@end defopt

